    "verdict_notes": "The paper calls SAE latents 'neurons', which could mislead keyword matching. None of its measures concern the base model's own neurons. The high identification rates (>97%) are pipeline summary-validity rates for SAE features. They are not evidence for V1's neuron-pole shares and are correctly left out as rows."
